{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/r1-correctness.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":949370,\"duration_api_ms\":950243,\"num_turns\":28,\"result\":\"I now have all information needed. Let me compile the analysis and produce the findings report.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"BLOCK\\\",\\n  \\\"lens\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n  \\\"slice\\\": \\\"WP-SCP-024 024B-extras\\\",\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"R8-CORR-001 (cascade-status regex), R8-CORR-002 (restore-mode guard scoping), plus all four prior-round MAJ findings (awk boundary match CORR-001, untested mutex guards CORR-002, workflow paths conflict CORR-003, dead if/else CORR-004) are verified closed. One new CRIT blocks merge: GATE2_CAUTION_LINE at enable-required-check.sh:505 expands ${OPERATOR} which is not initialized until line 803; under set -euo pipefail every invocation with --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification crashes with 'OPERATOR: unbound variable' before any API call. The Gate 3 bypass escape hatch is completely unusable and has no test covering the reachable code path. Two new MAJ findings: validate_restore_source_json requires required_status_checks to be a dict, but the GitHub API returns null when branch protection exists with no status checks configured—this pre-state would fail validation before posture-degradation guards are reached; and ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 3 shows only a flag fragment, not a copy-paste invocation, violating the break-glass procedure's concreteness requirement. Two MIN carry-forwards remain open: the dual required_signatures computation (Python + jq from prior CORR-005) and the actions/checkout SHA comment citing a non-existent v6.0.2 release. One nit carried from prior CORR-006: DISPATCH-NOTE code-span prevents machine parsing.\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-R3-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"CRIT\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"GATE2_CAUTION_LINE at enable-required-check.sh:505 expands ${OPERATOR} before OPERATOR is initialized at line 803. Under set -euo pipefail, any invocation with --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification exits immediately with 'OPERATOR: unbound variable'. The gate-3 bypass flag is unusable in production.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh:503-506 — if [ \\\\\\\"$ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION\\\\\\\" -eq 1 ]; then GATE2_CAUTION_LINE=\\\\\\\"...@${OPERATOR}...\\\\\\\"; fi. OPERATOR is not in the initialization block (lines 112-130) and not set until line 803. No test in the suite exercises --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification in a path that reaches line 504; the only test (line 2379) exits at the mutex check (line 246-249) before line 503.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Every Gate 3 re-enable invocation that uses the --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification escape hatch fails immediately with a shell error, making the ADOPT-001 §12.8 emergency bypass unreachable. A restore-followed-by-re-enable break-glass sequence cannot complete.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Initialize OPERATOR before line 503 (e.g., move the gh api user login call to the initialization block, or use OPERATOR=${OPERATOR:-} to default to empty, then populate at line 803). Add a test: run_enable_case with valid prior restore evidence + valid tag SHA + --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification → exit 0 + 'CAUTION' in stdout and 'Gate 2 verification bypassed' in log.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-R3-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"validate_restore_source_json requires required_status_checks to be a Python dict. The GitHub branch-protection GET API returns required_status_checks: null when protection exists but no checks are configured. A pre-state captured from such a repo fails validation with 'unexpected type' before reaching posture-degradation guards.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh:340-351 — required_types = {'required_status_checks': dict, ...}; isinstance(None, dict) is False → exits 2. The GitHub API for a branch with reviews but no status checks returns {\\\\\\\"required_status_checks\\\\\\\": null}. No test fixture has required_status_checks: null; all fixtures use a dict with contexts array.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"An adopter repo that had branch protection without required status checks before forward-mode enablement cannot be restored: the pre-state JSON that enable-required-check.sh would have logged contains required_status_checks: null and is rejected. The --restore flow is unusable for this class of adopter pre-state.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Change the required_types entry to 'required_status_checks': (dict, type(None)) and add a transform branch: if the key is required_status_checks and value is None, emit the PUT-compatible shape {\\\\\\\"strict\\\\\\\": false, \\\\\\\"contexts\\\\\\\": []}. Add a test with required_status_checks: null in pre-state.json expecting exit 0 + posture-degradation guard fires for empty contexts.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-R3-003\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"No test covers the --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification flag in a valid forward-mode flow (prior restore evidence present + valid release-tag SHA + bypass flag → expect exit 0 with CAUTION line). The only test touching the flag (line 2379) exits at the mutex check before line 504 is reached.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:2349-2379 — tests are: (a) arbitrary SHA not in tag cache → exit 2; (b) --expected-wrapper-sha + --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci mutex → exit 2. Neither reaches check_forward_mode_safety(). GATE2_CAUTION_LINE emission path (lines 503-506, 866) is uncovered.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"If CORR-R3-001 is fixed, the bypass flow is still not regression-guarded. Any future refactor of the gate-3 logic could silently break the escape hatch. The CAUTION line audit surface is untested.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"After fixing CORR-R3-001: add run_enable_case with a fake_gh that has prior restore evidence for jrnb2024/pim@main and a tag v1.2.3 → sha match; pass --expected-wrapper-sha <tag-sha> --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification. Assert exit 0 and that 'Gate 2 verification bypassed' or 'CAUTION' appears in stdout.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-R3-004\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 3 (line 1226-1228) presents only a flag fragment (--expected-wrapper-sha <release-tag-sha-from-Gate-2>) rather than a copy-paste invocation. The --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification bypass variant is described in WARNING/CAUTION prose but never shown as a concrete command.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1226-1228 — the bash code block contains only '--expected-wrapper-sha <release-tag-sha-from-Gate-2>' with no scripts/enable-required-check.sh --repo ... --branch ... prefix. Gate 1 and Gate 2 both show complete commands. DISPATCH-NOTE AC: 'concrete tag-SHA resolution commands; WARNING + CAUTION callouts for escape hatches'.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"In a time-pressured break-glass scenario, operators must mentally assemble the Gate 3 command from Gate 1's shape and Gate 3's flag fragment. The escape hatch variant has no example at all, increasing the risk of operator error or hesitation during outage.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Expand Gate 3 to a full command block: scripts/enable-required-check.sh --repo <owner/repo> --branch <branch> --expected-wrapper-sha <sha-from-Gate-2>. Add a second variant block with --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification in place of --expected-wrapper-sha, preceded by the WARNING callout.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-R3-005\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"check-invocation-log-entry.yml uses actions/checkout@de0fac2e4500dabe0009e67214ff5f5447ce83dd # v6.0.2. actions/checkout has no v6.x release (current is v4.x). The comment is incorrect; if the SHA does not exist in the actions/checkout repo, every CI run for this workflow fails at action download.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"check-invocation-log-entry.yml:32 — uses: actions/checkout@de0fac2e4500dabe0009e67214ff5f5447ce83dd # v6.0.2. Per D-038, SHA pins are mandatory supply-chain hardening, but the comment must be accurate so future maintainers can verify the pin. actions/checkout latest is v4.2.x as of the knowledge cutoff.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Misleading comment reduces auditability of the supply-chain pin. If the SHA was never committed to actions/checkout, the workflow silently fails CI on first PR that triggers it, blocking all cohort cascade PRs (024C–F) from receiving the invocation-log gate.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Verify sha de0fac2e exists in actions/checkout; correct the comment to the matching version tag (e.g., # v4.2.0 or # v4.x.y). Use a known valid pin such as the SHA for actions/checkout@v4.2.2 (@11bd71901bbe5b1630ceea73d27597364c9af683).\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-R3-006\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"RESTORE_SIGNATURES_ENABLED (line 609, Python) and restore_signatures_enabled (line 663, jq) derive the same required_signatures state from the same source JSON via two independent code paths. A future change to the pre-state shape could diverge silently.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh:609 — RESTORE_SIGNATURES_ENABLED via Python bool((data.get('required_signatures') or {}).get('enabled', False)). Line 663 — restore_signatures_enabled via jq '.required_signatures.enabled // false'. RESTORE_SIGNATURES_ENABLED is used in verify (line 741); restore_signatures_enabled drives the POST/DELETE decision (line 664). Carried forward from prior-round CORR-005.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Currently produces identical results. If required_signatures schema changes (e.g., becomes a top-level boolean), apply and verify could diverge, resulting in a POST/DELETE decision that contradicts the verify assertion and a silent partial-state failure.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Remove the jq computation at line 663 and reuse RESTORE_SIGNATURES_ENABLED throughout the restore apply block. One source of truth; the test at line 1747 already validates POST invocation from the Python-computed value.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-R3-007\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"DISPATCH-NOTE.md line 9 wraps cascade-status in a markdown code-span (` `cascade-status: not applicable` `), making it non-parseable by check-invocation-log-entry.sh's ^cascade-status: regex.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"DISPATCH-NOTE.md:9 — `` `cascade-status: not applicable` — this slice ships rollback... ``. Python regex r'^cascade-status:\\\\\\\\s+([^\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n]+?)\\\\\\\\s*$' with re.M: a line starting with backtick does not match. Script would exit 1 with 'expected exactly one cascade-status match, found 0' on direct CLI invocation. Carried forward from prior-round CORR-006.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"No CI failure since the workflow job-body short-circuits on 024B-extras. Confusing operator experience if check-invocation-log-entry.sh is ever invoked manually against this DISPATCH-NOTE.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add an unquoted machine-parseable header line: cascade-status: not applicable (no backticks). The existing prose description on line 9 can remain; the unquoted line satisfies both the machine parser and the human reader.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"carry_forward_verification\\\": {\\n    \\\"R8-CORR-001\\\": \\\"VERIFIED CLOSED — check-invocation-log-entry.sh:157-172 uses re.findall(r'^cascade-status:\\\\\\\\s+([^\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n]+?)\\\\\\\\s*$', text, re.M) with closed-set case statement validation; no trailing-prose capture possible.\\\",\\n    \\\"R8-CORR-002\\\": \\\"VERIFIED CLOSED — check_forward_mode_safety() is invoked only at enable-required-check.sh:515-517 behind 'if [ \\\\\\\"$RESTORE_MODE\\\\\\\" -eq 0 ]'; prior_restore_evidence_present() has no call site in restore mode.\\\",\\n    \\\"R8-CORR-003\\\": \\\"VERIFIED CLOSED IN 024B-CORE — n/a for this slice.\\\",\\n    \\\"R7_bootstrap_defect\\\": \\\"VERIFIED CLOSED — workflow paths-ignore: 024[AB]*/** prevents tooling-slice DISPATCH-NOTEs from triggering; job-body case exits 0 for 024A|024B-core|024B-extras|024G; awk target-anchored regex (boundary class [^A-Za-z0-9._/-]) confirmed preventing false-positive on REPO@main-legacy; test enable-target-anchored at line 2161 covers this.\\\",\\n    \\\"prior_CORR-001_awk_boundary\\\": \\\"VERIFIED CLOSED — enable-required-check.sh:414 now uses pat = \\\\\\\"(^|[^A-Za-z0-9._/-])\\\\\\\" target \\\\\\\"([^A-Za-z0-9._/-]|$)\\\\\\\" with match(); hyphen is in the allowed-char class so @main-legacy does not match @main boundary. Test at line 2226 (run_enable_case exit 0) confirms no false trigger.\\\",\\n    \\\"prior_CORR-002_untested_mutex\\\": \\\"VERIFIED CLOSED — test:1858-1862 now includes all five --restore mutex assertions: --plan, --no-enforce-admins, --i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate, --expected-wrapper-sha, --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci.\\\",\\n    \\\"prior_CORR-003_workflow_paths\\\": \\\"VERIFIED CLOSED — check-invocation-log-entry.yml paths-ignore contains only 024[AB]*/**; branch-protection-log.md and STATUS.md are NOT in paths-ignore, eliminating the conflicting-entry dead-rule issue.\\\",\\n    \\\"prior_CORR-004_dead_ifelse\\\": \\\"VERIFIED CLOSED — run_restore_case at test:365-420 and run_enable_case at test:422-476 both unconditionally shift 5 with no dead if/else.\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"8a2cdea8-0bcd-4f9c-be66-50cd672053f8\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.7456266999999996,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":20,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":142088,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":1493554,\"output_tokens\":49771,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":142088,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":11281,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":150284,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":3511,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":3511},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":1753,\"outputTokens\":26,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.001883,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":20,\"outputTokens\":49771,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":1493554,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":146414,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.7437436999999998,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"c9ca0a9e-553b-4dc1-b147-fce8801a39d3\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
