{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/r1-safety_bypass.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":660148,\"duration_api_ms\":660638,\"num_turns\":22,\"result\":\"I have all the information needed. Here is the structured findings report:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"BLOCK\\\",\\n  \\\"lens\\\": \\\"safety_bypass\\\",\\n  \\\"slice\\\": \\\"WP-SCP-024 024B-extras\\\",\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"R8-SAFE-001 (--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification WARNING + CAUTION callouts), R8-SAFE-002 (working-tree diff added to prior-entry detection), and R8-Bootstrap (paths-ignore + job-body short-circuit) are verified closed. One new CRIT blocks merge: GATE2_CAUTION_LINE at enable-required-check.sh:503-506 expands ${OPERATOR} before OPERATOR is initialised at line 803; under set -euo pipefail every invocation with --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification aborts with 'OPERATOR: unbound variable' before any API mutation or log emission — the escape hatch is inoperative and leaves no audit trail. Four MAJ findings: the Gate 3 sha-pin requirement can be bypassed by committing a deletion of the 'Restoring TO:' restore-evidence entry (prior_restore_evidence_present reads the current working-tree file, not git HEAD); restore-mode tests invoke enable-required-check.sh which exits 1 under GITHUB_ACTIONS=true so the entire restore test suite fails silently in CI; validate_restore_source_json rejects required_status_checks:null with exit 2, blocking rollback of a valid pre-state class where the adopter had no configured status checks; and the --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification happy-path test is absent, leaving the escape hatch behaviour unguarded post-fix. Two MIN findings: tag-list pagination is capped at 100 making large-estate gate-3 re-enables rejectable, and ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 3 shows only a flag fragment rather than a full invocation command. No descoping recommended.\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-R3-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"CRIT\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"${OPERATOR} is referenced at enable-required-check.sh:505 inside the GATE2_CAUTION_LINE assignment before OPERATOR is initialised (line 803). Under set -euo pipefail, passing --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification aborts with 'OPERATOR: unbound variable' before any API call or log emission.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh:503-506 — if [ \\\\\\\"$ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION\\\\\\\" -eq 1 ]; then GATE2_CAUTION_LINE=\\\\\\\"...Operator @${OPERATOR}...\\\\\\\"; fi. OPERATOR appears in no initialisation block (lines 112-130) and is first assigned at line 803 via gh api user. The only test touching the flag (test:2379) exits at the mutex guard (line 246) well before line 503 is reached.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Every Gate 3 re-enable using the escape hatch immediately crashes the script. No branch-protection mutation occurs, no CAUTION audit line is emitted, and the break-glass procedure documented in ADOPT-001 §12.8 is unreachable. D-047 rationale 'escape hatch is explicitly auditable' is false.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Initialise OPERATOR=\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\" at the top of the script (alongside REPO, BRANCH) so nounset does not fire. Populate the real value via 'gh api user' at line 803 as today; move GATE2_CAUTION_LINE assembly to AFTER that call (or use OPERATOR=${OPERATOR:-unresolved} as a safe default). Add a test: run_enable_case with prior restore evidence + valid tag SHA + --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification → exit 0 with 'Gate 2 verification bypassed' or 'CAUTION' in stdout.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-R3-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Gate 3's --expected-wrapper-sha requirement can be bypassed by committing a deletion of the 'Restoring TO:' log entry. prior_restore_evidence_present() reads the current working-tree file via 'cat \\\\\\\"$log_path\\\\\\\"', not the git-HEAD committed content. After the entry is committed-deleted from branch-protection-log.md, the function returns false and Gate 3 allows re-enable without sha-pin validation.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh:407-413 — committed_blob=\\\\\\\"$(cat \\\\\\\"$log_path\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\"; working_tree_diff=\\\\\\\"$(git diff HEAD -- \\\\\\\"$log_path\\\\\\\" ...)\\\\\\\". If the deletion is committed, HEAD no longer has 'Restoring TO:' and git diff HEAD is empty, so both sources are clean. check_forward_mode_safety:479-484 — guard only fires when prior_restore_evidence_present returns true. No test covers the committed-deletion scenario.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"An operator can remove the integrity anchor by committing a 'log cleanup' PR, then re-enable against any SHA without tag validation. Intended break-glass Gate 2 sha-pin discipline is circumvented. In single-operator mode (D-031) this requires self-merge through branch protection, but is achievable.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Replace the 'cat' read with a git-history search: use 'git log --all -p -- \\\\\\\"$log_path\\\\\\\" | grep -q \\\\\\\"Restoring TO:\\\\\\\"' or walk committed revisions of the log file rather than the current working-tree state. Alternatively, also scan 'git log -p -- \\\\\\\"$log_path\\\\\\\"' output (committed history) and short-circuit on any committed line containing target + Restoring TO. Add a test that commits a log deletion and verifies prior_restore_evidence_present still returns true.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-R3-003\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"run_restore_case and run_enable_case in test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh invoke enable-required-check.sh which exits 1 when GITHUB_ACTIONS=true. The test harness does not unset GITHUB_ACTIONS. When the test suite runs in GitHub Actions CI, every restore and enable test assertion fails with wrong exit code (1 instead of 0 or 2), leaving all restore safety properties unvalidated by CI.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh:62-66 — 'if [ \\\\\\\"${CI:-}\\\\\\\" = \\\\\\\"true\\\\\\\" ] || [ \\\\\\\"${GITHUB_ACTIONS:-}\\\\\\\" = \\\\\\\"true\\\\\\\" ]; then echo refuses to run in CI; exit 1; fi'. test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:375-420 run_restore_case and 422-476 run_enable_case both subshell-exec RESTORE_SCRIPT with only PATH= override; GITHUB_ACTIONS is inherited from caller. check-invocation-log-entry.yml runs on ubuntu-24.04 where GITHUB_ACTIONS=true.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"The CI run of the test suite reports all restore/enable assertions as FAIL (exit code mismatch: expected 0 or 2, got 1) or silently skips them if the harness absorbs the failure. No restore safety property — APPLY_FAIL pattern, posture-degradation flags, sha-pin validation, required_signatures POST/DELETE — is regression-guarded in CI.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"In run_restore_case and run_enable_case, unset GITHUB_ACTIONS and CI inside the subshell before invoking RESTORE_SCRIPT: '(cd \\\\\\\"$repo_dir\\\\\\\" && unset CI GITHUB_ACTIONS && PATH=... \\\\\\\"$RESTORE_SCRIPT\\\\\\\" ...)'. Alternatively add a test-only env override that the script recognises when a SCP_TEST_MODE=1 flag is set. Verify CI passes with all restore case exit-code assertions after the fix.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-R3-004\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"validate_restore_source_json requires required_status_checks to be a Python dict; the GitHub branch-protection GET API returns required_status_checks:null when branch protection exists but no status checks are configured. A pre-state captured from such a repo passes the BEFORE_JSON capture but then fails restore validation with exit 2, blocking rollback and violating the <30-min SLO.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh:340-351 — required_types = {'required_status_checks': dict, ...}; isinstance(None, dict) is False → sys.exit(2) with 'unexpected type'. GitHub REST API v3 branch-protection response can have required_status_checks:null for protected branches with reviews but no required checks. No test fixture uses required_status_checks:null.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"An adopter repo with no prior required checks (a common pre-onboarding state) cannot be rolled back: the pre-state JSON logged by forward-mode invocation is rejected at restore time. The invariant-7 rollback SLO fails for this class of adopter, which may be the majority of the cohort (024C-F).\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Change required_types entry to 'required_status_checks': (dict, type(None)) and add a transform branch for null: if value is None emit the PUT-safe shape {'strict': False, 'contexts': []}. Add the posture-degradation check for null (contexts=empty, guard fires). Add test fixture with required_status_checks:null expecting exit 0 after --i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-R3-005\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"No test covers the --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification happy-path (prior restore evidence present + valid release-tag SHA + bypass flag → exit 0 with CAUTION line). The only test mentioning the flag (line 2379) exits at the mutex check before line 503 is reached.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:2349-2379 — tests: (a) arbitrary SHA not in tag cache → exit 2; (b) --expected-wrapper-sha + --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci mutex → exit 2. Both abort before check_forward_mode_safety(). GATE2_CAUTION_LINE emission (lines 503-506, 867) and the CAUTION log in check_forward_mode_safety (lines 489-492) are unreachable from any existing test.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Post SAFE-R3-001 fix, the bypass flow has no regression guard. Any refactor of Gate 3 logic can silently re-break the escape hatch. The ADOPT-001 §12.8 emergency path remains unverified end-to-end.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"After fixing SAFE-R3-001: add run_enable_case with fake_gh having prior restore evidence for jrnb2024/pim@main, tags.json with v1.2.3, tag-refs/v1.2.3.json with SHA=aaaa...; pass --expected-wrapper-sha <sha> --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification. Assert exit 0. Assert 'Gate 2 verification bypassed' or 'CAUTION' appears in stdout. Assert no 'OPERATOR: unbound variable' in stderr.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-R3-006\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags fetches tag refs with per_page=100 and no pagination. If the SCP repo acquires >100 tags (plausible across 024C-024F + version bumps + pre-release tags), valid release-tag SHAs beyond the first 100 are silently missing from the cache and rejected with exit 2, blocking Gate 3 re-enable.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh:435 — gh api 'repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-/git/refs/tags?per_page=100'. No follow-on pagination loop. GitHub REST API paginates at per_page ceiling; tags beyond page 1 are not fetched. Fails safe (rejects rather than accepts) but breaks legitimate emergency recovery.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Legitimate Gate 3 re-enable fails with 'SHA not found in release-tag SHA cache' when the SCP repo exceeds 100 tags, forcing operator to use the --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification escape hatch (itself broken per SAFE-R3-001). Emergency recovery SLO is doubly degraded.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a pagination loop: fetch next page via Link header until all tags are retrieved, or use GraphQL refs API with cursor. Alternatively cap the design at per_page=100 and document the <100-tag estate assumption explicitly in the script comment as a known limitation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-R3-007\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 3 (line 1226-1228) shows only '--expected-wrapper-sha <release-tag-sha-from-Gate-2>' without the enclosing scripts/enable-required-check.sh --repo ... --branch ... prefix. The --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification bypass variant has no concrete command example at all, only WARNING/CAUTION prose.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1222-1228 — Gate 1 bash block shows full command; Gate 2 bash block shows full gh api command; Gate 3 bash block contains only '--expected-wrapper-sha ...' flag fragment. Lines 1232-1234 describe the bypass flag in prose but provide no copy-pasteable invocation.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"In a time-pressured outage, operators must assemble the Gate 3 invocation mentally from Gate 1's shape + Gate 3's flag fragment. The bypass variant (the most likely path when sha-pin infrastructure itself is broken) has no example, increasing the risk of operator hesitation or invocation error during the <30-min rollback SLO window.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Expand Gate 3 to a full command block: scripts/enable-required-check.sh --repo <owner/repo> --branch <branch> --expected-wrapper-sha <sha-from-Gate-2>. Add a second code block for the bypass variant: scripts/enable-required-check.sh --repo ... --branch ... --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification, preceded by the WARNING callout. Match the completeness of Gates 1 and 2.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"carry_forward_verification\\\": {\\n    \\\"R8-SAFE-001\\\": \\\"VERIFIED CLOSED — ADOPT-001 §12.8:1232-1234 contains WARNING and CAUTION callouts for --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification; enable-required-check.sh:503-506 emits GATE2_CAUTION_LINE in the log block (though the emission is broken by SAFE-R3-001); check_forward_mode_safety:489 emits 'CAUTION: Gate 2 verification bypassed' via log(); D-047 rationale acknowledges escape hatch.\\\",\\n    \\\"R8-SAFE-002\\\": \\\"VERIFIED CLOSED — prior_restore_evidence_present() at enable-required-check.sh:406-430 correctly combines 'cat \\\\\\\"$log_path\\\\\\\"' (working tree) with 'git diff HEAD -- \\\\\\\"$log_path\\\\\\\"' (uncommitted changes); awk strips +/- diff prefixes so added restore entries in the working-tree diff are detected. Test enable-working-tree-prior-restore at test:2228-2294 exercises this path. NOTE: SAFE-R3-002 is a separate gap — committed deletions bypass the check.\\\",\\n    \\\"R8-Bootstrap\\\": \\\"VERIFIED CLOSED — check-invocation-log-entry.yml paths-ignore: docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[AB]*/** correctly excludes 024B-extras slice files; job body case statement exits 0 for 024A|024B-core|024B-extras|024G; STATUS.md in paths triggers workflow but job short-circuits on tooling-slice DISPATCH-NOTE. Both layers provide defense-in-depth.\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"fd276218-0a30-47c4-8bde-bb2c360e219d\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.3347641,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1078,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":137120,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":1176137,\"output_tokens\":30847,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":137120,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":6364,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":139845,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":4656,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":4656},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":1669,\"outputTokens\":23,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.001784,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":1078,\"outputTokens\":30847,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":1176137,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":137120,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.3329801,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"f1b87441-54e8-429c-819a-494b4a24c082\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
