{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/r1-completeness_governance.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":452104,\"duration_api_ms\":453199,\"num_turns\":23,\"result\":\"I now have all the information needed to produce the structured review. Let me emit the findings JSON.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"reviewer_lens\\\": \\\"COMPLETENESS_GOVERNANCE\\\",\\n  \\\"slice_id\\\": \\\"WP-SCP-024/024B-extras\\\",\\n  \\\"review_round\\\": \\\"R1\\\",\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"CONDITIONAL_APPROVE\\\",\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"024B-extras delivers --restore mode, ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass, and CI workflow wiring against plan-doc invariants 7 and 2. Carry-forward findings from extras-parking R8 are addressed: R8-SAFE-001 (WARNING + CAUTION callouts present in §12.8 and log block), R8-SAFE-002 (working-tree diff detection in prior_restore_evidence_present verified), R8 bootstrap (paths-ignore 024[AB]*/** + job-body short-circuit confirmed). D-047 mirrors D-044 format, is filed at dispatch date, and acknowledges the --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification escape hatch and bootstrap paths-ignore. TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001 is filed in STATUS.md; the step-7 demo AC correctly remains unchecked at R1. VERSIONING.md protected flag list covers four of the five new flags. STATUS.md chain entry documents outcome and parking-branch closure note. Plan-doc §6 correctly gates 024C on both 024B halves plus FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001. Three MAJ findings require fixes: (1) --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci missing from VERSIONING.md breaking-change surface; (2) forward-mode safety check failure paths entirely absent from tests, violating the 'tests cover forward-mode safety check' AC; (3) --restore + --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification silently accepted without incompatibility guard, creating misleading audit posture during break-glass. Two MIN findings: workflow paths-ignore deviates from DISPATCH-NOTE spec; TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001 references the wrong evidence file path. Anti-descoping check passed: all original 024B-extras scope items are present; step-7 demo is the sole merge-blocking operator-interactive AC.\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"MAJ-CG-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci is absent from VERSIONING.md §Branch-protection helper protected flag removal list. It is a new flag from 024B-extras scope (forward-mode safety check cold-start bypass) but is not enumerated alongside the other nine protected flags.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"VERSIONING.md §Branch-protection helper lists exactly 10 flags including --restore, --expected-wrapper-sha, --i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement, --i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks, --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification — but not --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci. Flag parsed at enable-required-check.sh line 204; referenced in DISPATCH-NOTE scope table forward-mode safety check row.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"If this flag is removed in a future PATCH or MINOR release, VERSIONING.md does not require a breaking-change bump. Cold-start adopters relying on the bypass would silently break without a deprecation ramp.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci` to the flag list in VERSIONING.md §Branch-protection helper. No other changes required.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"MAJ-CG-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"AC states 'tests cover forward-mode safety check' but tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh has zero test coverage for the three forward-mode safety check failure paths: (a) no wrapper workflow found → exit 2, (b) no successful runs in 60 days → exit 2, (c) --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci bypass in forward-mode → exit 0 despite empty runs.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"All run_enable_case invocations (enable-expected-sha, enable-expected-sha-cross-target, enable-target-anchored, enable-working-tree-prior-restore, enable-expected-sha-arbitrary, enable-sha-mutex) use fixtures with a wrapper workflow present and runs-2.json non-empty. No run_enable_case test sets workflows.json to empty-set or runs-2.json to {workflow_runs:[]} to exercise the fail-closed paths.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Regressions in check_forward_mode_safety() — the new safety check that closes the 'no enable before wrapper CI-greens' foot-gun — will not be caught by the test suite. The AC coverage claim is incorrect, and CI green does not prove forward-mode safety check correctness.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add three run_enable_case test cases: (a) workflows.json omits policy-check-wrapper.yml → expect exit 2 'no workflow with path'; (b) runs-2.json={workflow_runs:[]} → expect exit 2 'no successful workflow runs'; (c) runs-2.json empty + --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci → expect exit 0 with 'safety check bypassed' log line.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"MAJ-CG-003\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"--restore combined with --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification is silently accepted without incompatibility error. The flag is semantically a Gate-3/forward-mode flag; accepting it in restore mode creates misleading operator state and no audit CAUTION is emitted.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh lines 219-244 check restore-mode incompatibilities for --plan, --no-enforce-admins, --i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate, --expected-wrapper-sha, --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci — but NOT ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION. GATE2_CAUTION_LINE is set at line 503-506 but the restore log block (lines 814-847) never emits it; the flag has no effect. No test asserts this combination fails.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"An operator running --restore --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification during an emergency may believe they have acknowledged Gate 2 bypass during the restore operation. The flag silently has no effect; audit trail omits the expected CAUTION line; operator mental model of break-glass state is wrong.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add to the restore-mode incompatibility block (lines 219-244): if ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION -eq 1, exit 2 'cannot be combined with --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification in restore mode'. Add a corresponding run_restore_case test. The flag is only meaningful in forward-mode Gate-3 re-enable.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"MIN-CG-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"CI workflow paths-ignore deviates from DISPATCH-NOTE spec. DISPATCH-NOTE scope table specifies paths-ignore includes docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md and STATUS.md, but the actual workflow places those paths in the trigger's paths block instead, not in paths-ignore.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"DISPATCH-NOTE scope table: 'paths-ignore: [docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[AB]*/**, docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md, STATUS.md]'. Actual check-invocation-log-entry.yml: paths-ignore contains only docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[AB]*/**; branch-protection-log.md and STATUS.md appear under paths (trigger). Job-body short-circuit exits 0 when no cascade-slice DISPATCH-NOTE is in the diff.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"PRs that modify only STATUS.md or branch-protection-log.md (e.g. status update PRs, log commits) trigger the workflow unnecessarily and consume a required-status check slot. Behavior is functionally correct (exits 0 via short-circuit) but creates CI noise and deviates from stated design.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Move docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md and STATUS.md from paths to paths-ignore. Cohort cascade PRs already trigger via docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[C-Z]*/**; the job-body short-circuit remains as defense-in-depth.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"MIN-CG-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001 in STATUS.md references restore-roundtrip-evidence.md (without PLACEHOLDER suffix) while DISPATCH-NOTE AC and STATUS.md 2026-05-10 chain row 4 reference restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md. Inconsistent paths across tracking artefacts.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"STATUS.md TF entry: 'docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence.md'. DISPATCH-NOTE AC: 'docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md'. STATUS.md chain row 4: 'placeholder path recorded at docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md'.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Operator completing the demo may commit evidence to the wrong path (no PLACEHOLDER suffix), leaving the placeholder file unconsumed; or may rename -PLACEHOLDER.md thinking TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001's path is the target. AC closure tracking is ambiguous.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Update TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001 to reference restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md as the current file and clarify that the operator replaces the placeholder file's content in-place (or replaces it) when committing real evidence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"nit-CG-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"GATE2_CAUTION_LINE is initialized at enable-required-check.sh line 503-506, before the restore-mode branch at line 515. In restore mode the variable is populated but never referenced in the restore log block (lines 814-847); only the forward-mode log block (line 867) uses it.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Line 503: 'GATE2_CAUTION_LINE=\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"'; lines 504-506: set if ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION=1. Restore log template (lines 814-847): no ${GATE2_CAUTION_LINE} interpolation. Forward-mode log template (line 867): '${GATE2_CAUTION_LINE}'. The variable is dead code in restore mode.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Cosmetic only; no behavior change. Restore log block correctly omits the caution line. Code is slightly confusing to readers who expect all initialization of forward-mode-only variables to live inside the forward-mode branch.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Move GATE2_CAUTION_LINE initialization into the else branch of the RESTORE_MODE guard (forward-mode only), or add an inline comment: '# used only in forward-mode log block below'.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"11ea0c69-bd2c-4356-a23e-12e4da76d98f\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.2784148499999999,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1079,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":135297,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":1390987,\"output_tokens\":23239,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":135297,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":20465,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":136929,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":5749,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":5749},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":1823,\"outputTokens\":22,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.001933,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":1079,\"outputTokens\":23239,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":1390987,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":135297,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.27648185,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"f4cbacdf-382e-4022-b54a-73dad2203905\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
